  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "When a task fails",
      "items": [
        "A failed result marks its host failed inside _process_pending_results, via iterator.mark_host_failed",
        "The failed host leaves the lockstep batch; the rescue and always sections of its block still run",
        "max_fail_percentage can end the whole play early, with the no-hosts-remaining callback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "The lockstep loop",
      "items": [
        "The linear strategy keeps every host on the same task: no host moves on until the current task is done",
        "TaskExecutor.run() delegates to _execute_internal(), which templates the task, sets up the connection and calls the action plugin",
        "A meta: flush_handlers task is inserted by Play.compile so handlers run at section boundaries",
        "Each task is a separate forked worker process; the controller keeps the shared result queue"
      ]
    }
  ]
